# EvalHub Reference Documentation

## Authoritative Sources

All decisions, configurations, and implementations related to EvalHub MUST be validated against these official sources:

1. **Documentation site:** https://eval-hub.github.io/
2. **GitHub organisation:** https://github.com/eval-hub
   - [eval-hub](https://github.com/eval-hub/eval-hub) — Go server (REST API, orchestration)
   - [eval-hub-sdk](https://github.com/eval-hub/eval-hub-sdk) — Python SDK, CLI, adapters
   - [eval-hub-contrib](https://github.com/eval-hub/eval-hub-contrib) — Community adapters

## When to Consult

Before making any of these changes, fetch the relevant page from the docs site:

- **API calls or endpoint changes** → [Server API Reference](https://eval-hub.github.io/reference/server-api/)
- **SDK / CLI usage** → [Python SDK](https://eval-hub.github.io/reference/python-sdk/) or [CLI Guide](https://eval-hub.github.io/guides/cli/)
- **Adapter configuration** → [Adapters section](https://eval-hub.github.io/adapters/guidellm/overview/)
- **Deployment on OpenShift** → [OpenShift Setup](https://eval-hub.github.io/deployment/openshift-setup/)
- **Architecture questions** → [System Overview](https://eval-hub.github.io/architecture/system-overview/)
- **Benchmark collections** → [LightEval Benchmarks](https://eval-hub.github.io/adapters/lighteval/benchmarks/)
- **MCP integration** → [MCP Overview](https://eval-hub.github.io/mcp/overview/)
- **Disconnected clusters** → [Disconnected Cluster Guide](https://eval-hub.github.io/guides/disconnected-cluster/)

## Validation Rules

1. **Do NOT guess** EvalHub API fields, adapter names, or benchmark identifiers — look them up.
2. **Use `context7` MCP** or `WebFetch` to retrieve current docs when implementing changes.
3. **Cite the source** in ADRs and commit messages when a decision is based on EvalHub docs.
4. **Supported adapters**: lm-eval-harness, LightEval, GuideLLM, Garak, MTEB, IBM CLEAR.
5. **Provider names** are specific strings (e.g. `lm_evaluation_harness`, `lighteval`, `guidellm`, `garak`, `mteb`, `ibm-clear`) — always verify against the docs.

## Key Architecture Facts

- Server is written in Go; SDK and adapters are Python.
- Each evaluation runs as an isolated Kubernetes Job.
- Results are stored as OCI artefacts; metrics go to MLflow.
- REST API is versioned (`/api/v1/`).
- Supports PostgreSQL or SQLite as backend database.
- Multi-tenancy via namespace-based isolation and Kubernetes RBAC.
